If a student is selected at random from those in 10th grade, what is the probability that the student prefers swimming?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{13}{27}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{13}{58}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{21}{58}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{9}{27}$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'A', NULL, E'The question asks for the probability of preferring swimming given that the student is in 10th grade, so the denominator is the total number of 10th-grade students, which is $27$, and the numerator is the $13$ who prefer swimming: $\\frac{13}{27}$. The value $\\frac{13}{58}$ incorrectly uses the total number of all students as the denominator instead of conditioning on 10th grade. The value $\\frac{21}{58}$ gives the overall probability of preferring swimming rather than the conditional probability for 10th graders. The value $\\frac{9}{27}$ reads the soccer column for 10th grade instead of the swimming column.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"concept_gap"},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"misread_question"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"graph_read_error"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 90, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-18"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-18","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);




$$\\begin{cases} x + y = 19 \\\\ x - y = 7 \\end{cases}$$', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$6$"},{"key":"B","text":"$13$"},{"key":"C","text":"$12$"},{"key":"D","text":"$26$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'A', NULL, E'Adding the two equations eliminates $y$: $(x + y) + (x - y) = 19 + 7$, giving $2x = 26$, so $x = 13$. Substituting into $x + y = 19$ yields $y = 6$. The value $13$ is the value of $x$, not $y$, resulting from misreading what the question asks. The value $12$ comes from computing $19 - 7 = 12$ without dividing by $2$. The value $26$ results from adding $19 + 7$ without recognizing that this sum equals $2x$, not $y$.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"misread_question"},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"arithmetic_slip"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"equation_setup_error"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 60, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-18"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-18","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);





$$\\begin{cases} 3x + ky = 17 \\\\ 9x + 21y = 40 \\end{cases}$$', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$3$"},{"key":"B","text":"$7$"},{"key":"C","text":"$9$"},{"key":"D","text":"$21$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'B', NULL, E'A system of two linear equations has no solution when the lines are parallel but not identical — that is, the ratios of the coefficients of $x$ and $y$ are equal, but the ratio of the constants is different. The ratio of the $x$-coefficients is $\\frac{3}{9} = \\frac{1}{3}$. For no solution, the $y$-coefficient ratio must also equal $\\frac{1}{3}$: $\\frac{k}{21} = \\frac{1}{3}$, so $k = 7$. Checking the constants: $\\frac{17}{40} \\neq \\frac{1}{3}$, confirming the lines are parallel but not identical, so the system has no solution. The value $3$ comes from using the $x$-coefficient of the first equation directly rather than computing the required ratio. The value $9$ results from confusing the $x$-coefficient of the second equation with the needed $k$. The value $21$ reflects a misunderstanding that matching the $y$-coefficient of the second equation produces parallel lines.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"},"B":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"equation_setup_error"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"concept_gap"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 120, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-18"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-18","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);










